# Phase 3 parity continuation — 2026-09-26T15:19:49Z

- Continued strict Java 5.5.1 parity audit; Phase 4 remains gated and no plan was modified.
- Java `TlsHelper.buildSslContext(true)` returns a trust-all client context before reading client CA/certificate/key paths or invoking the decryptor. Rust property loading previously attempted those reads even when `tls.test.mode.enable=true`, causing invalid but intentionally ignored files to fail client construction. Updated `TlsConfig::apply_properties` to read/decrypt client material only when test mode is disabled; adjusted connector selection so material is ignored in test mode as in Java. Added `java_tls_test_mode_ignores_client_material_and_decryption_strategy` covering missing paths and zero decryptor invocations. Updated the existing decryptor test to explicitly set verified mode.
- Focused TLS test initially identified the prior decryptor fixture's implicit dependence on default test mode; updated fixture to select verified mode, consistent with Java's test-mode early return. All four TLS unit tests then passed.
- Updated `docs/compatibility/PHASE_3_REMOTING_INVENTORY.md` and `docs/compatibility/JAVA_5_5_1_COMPATIBILITY.md` to state test-mode behavior and remaining TLS lifecycle gaps.
- Validation passed: `cargo fmt --all --check`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked --offline -- -D warnings`; `cargo test --workspace --locked --offline` (common 11, protocol 9 unit + 1 integration, remoting 30 unit + 4 codec + 63 transport); `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py`; `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`; `git diff --check`.
- No Java Maven/Broker/Docker/cross-language live validation performed. Phase 3 remains unaccepted; many inventory blockers remain. TLS fix committed as `1678cb7`.
- Continued audit found Rust's Java-properties unescaper rejected UTF-16 surrogate halves, whereas Java `Properties.load` combines `\\uD83D\\uDE80` into one supplementary Unicode character. Added surrogate-pair decoding and test `java_tls_properties_decode_surrogate_pair_unicode_escapes`; targeted test passes. Updated TLS property inventory. This follow-up is pending full workspace gates and commit.
